      "text": "Let \\( x \\) and \\( y \\) be the two positive real numbers. The geometric mean of \\( x \\) and \\( y \\) is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{xy} = \\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\nSquaring both sides, we get:\n\n\\[\nxy = 3\n\\]\n\nThe harmonic mean of \\( x \\) and \\( y \\) is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{2xy}{x+y} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\( xy = 3 \\) into the harmonic mean formula, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{2 \\cdot 3}{x+y} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the left side, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{6}{x+y} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\n\nCross-multiplying gives:\n\n\\[\n6 \\cdot 2 = 3 \\cdot (x + y)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n12 = 3(x + y)\n\\]\n\nDividing both sides by 3 gives:\n\n\\[\nx + y = 4\n\\]\n\nNow, we have two equations:\n\n1. \\( xy = 3 \\)\n2. \\( x + y = 4 \\)\n\nWe can treat \\( x \\) and \\( y \\) as the roots of a quadratic equation. The quadratic equation whose roots are \\( x \\) and \\( y \\) is:\n\n\\[\nt^2 - (x+y)t + xy = 0\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\( x + y = 4 \\) and \\( xy = 3 \\), we get:\n\n\\[\nt^2 - 4t + 3 = 0\n\\]\n\nWe solve this quadratic equation by factoring:\n\n\\[\n(t-1)(t-3) = 0\n\\]\n\nThus, the roots are \\( t = 1 \\) and \\( t = 3 \\). Therefore, the two numbers are 1 and 3. Putting the final answer in the required format, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1, 3}\n\\]",
